{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.MarkovTraceOnHecke","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovTraceOnHecke","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Fin","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fin.VecNotation","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FinCases"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.markovTrace_realized","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.markovTrace_realized","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTraceOnHecke.lean#L224-L234","doc":"The concrete n=3 trace is a **real** linear functional satisfying the\nMarkov **trace** laws — no longer a `True` marker. Bundles (M1) linearity,\n(M2) cyclicity, and (M3) the Markov reduction; the bridge for discharging\n`markov_trace_origin` once Step 4 names the residue-A element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.trM_cyclic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.trM_cyclic","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTraceOnHecke.lean#L210-L222","doc":"**(M2) Trace cyclicity** `tr_M(u · v) = tr_M(v · u)` — the defining\nproperty of a *trace*, here for the full `H₃(q)` algebra product `mulNF`.\nThis is what makes `trM` an honest Markov **trace** (not merely a Markov-\nreducible functional), and it is exactly the symmetry the `Ind_{H₃}^{H₄}`\nMarkov-stabilization analysis relies on. Verified over `ℚ(z,h)` by the\nsymbolic preflight before being formalized; the identity is a polynomial\nin the entries of `u`, `v` and the parameters `z, h`, closed by `ring`\nafter the trace sum and the nested `mulσ` actions are unfolded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.trM_markov_σ₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.trM_markov_σ₁","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTraceOnHecke.lean#L201-L208","doc":"**(M3) Markov reduction** `tr(x·σ₁) = z·tr(x)` for\n`x ∈ H₂ = span{γ, σ₀}` (i.e. `v 2 = v 3 = v 4 = v 5 = 0`). The defining\nMarkov property at the `H₂ ↪ H₃` inclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.mulσ₀_hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.mulσ₀_hecke","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTraceOnHecke.lean#L194-L199","doc":"**(M3) Hecke relation** as an operator identity: `σ₀² = h·σ₀ + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.trM_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.trM_smul","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTraceOnHecke.lean#L188-L192","doc":"**(M1) Linearity** — homogeneity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.trM_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.trM_add","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTraceOnHecke.lean#L183-L186","doc":"**(M1) Linearity** — additivity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.mulNF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.mulNF","kind":"def","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTraceOnHecke.lean#L157-L181","doc":"The **full algebra product** `u · v` on the NF free module of `H₃(q)`.\n\nEach basis element `b_j` is the GB normal form of a generator word `W_j`,\nand right-multiplication is an anti-homomorphism `R_{ab} = R_b ∘ R_a`, so\n`u · b_j = R_{W_j}(u)` is the composite of `mulσ₀`/`mulσ₁` along `W_j`. By\nright-linearity `u · v = ∑_j v_j · (u · b_j)`. The producing words (and\nhence the composition order — note `b₃ = σ₁σ₀`, `b₄ = σ₀σ₁`) were pinned by\nthe symbolic preflight in `gram.py`'s `hm` convention, which also verified\n`tr_M(u·v) = tr_M(v·u)` as an identity over `ℚ(z,h)`:\n\n| `j` | basis `b_j` | word `W_j` | `u · b_j` |\n|----|------------|-----------|-----------|\n| 0 | `γ`  | `()`      | `u` |\n| 1 | `σ₀` | `(0)`     | `mulσ₀ u` |\n| 2 | `σ₁` | `(1)`     | `mulσ₁ u` |\n| 3 | `L₊` | `(1,0)`   | `mulσ₀ (mulσ₁ u)` |\n| 4 | `L₋` | `(0,1)`   | `mulσ₁ (mulσ₀ u)` |\n| 5 | `e⁻` | `(0,1,0)` | `mulσ₀ (mulσ₁ (mulσ₀ u))` | ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.mulσ₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.mulσ₁","kind":"def","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTraceOnHecke.lean#L153-L155","doc":"Right action of `σ₁` on the NF basis (mirrors `gram.hm(·,1,0,1)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.mulσ₀","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.mulσ₀","kind":"def","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTraceOnHecke.lean#L149-L151","doc":"Right action of `σ₀` on the NF basis (mirrors `gram.hm(·,1,0,0)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.trM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.trM","kind":"def","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTraceOnHecke.lean#L144-L147","doc":"The **Markov trace** on the NF free module `Fin 6 → R`: the linear\nfunctional `v ↦ ∑ᵢ vᵢ · TRMᵢ`. The real structure behind the `True`\nmarker. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.TRM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.TRM","kind":"def","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTraceOnHecke.lean#L138-L142","doc":"Markov-Ocneanu-Wenzl weights on the GB-NF basis `[γ, σ₀, σ₁, L₊, L₋,\ne⁻]` of `H₃(q)` (mirrors `gram.TR_M` / `trace_formal.TR_M_formal`):\n`tr_M(e⁻) = h·z² + z` — the 2026-05-19 fix, NOT `z³`. `z` is the Markov\nparameter, `h = q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.ResidueACompositeIdentification.composite_markov_residue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.ResidueACompositeIdentification.composite_markov_residue","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTraceOnHecke.lean#L122-L122","doc":"Composite Wenzl × Demazure operator has well-defined Markov-trace\nresidue at `u_substrate` (opaque marker for the open derivation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.ResidueACompositeIdentification.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.ResidueACompositeIdentification.mk","kind":"ctor","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTraceOnHecke.lean#L119-L119","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.ResidueACompositeIdentification","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.ResidueACompositeIdentification","kind":"class","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTraceOnHecke.lean#L111-L122","doc":"Conditional class for the residue A composite identification.\nNEAR-MATCH tier; instance not constructed (requires upstream Wenzl,\nMarkov trace, and Demazure-crystal infrastructure to be in place).\n\nThe composite operator is `(Wenzl projector p_3) × (Demazure char χ_λ)`,\nevaluated at proton-pinned q₀; the Markov-trace residue at the\n`u_substrate` pole is conjecturally `A = c_3 (Hopf-Jones value) +\nq-Pochhammer correction`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.JonesWenzlProjector.idempotent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.JonesWenzlProjector.idempotent","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTraceOnHecke.lean#L101-L101","doc":"Idempotence of the projector: `p · p = p`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.JonesWenzlProjector.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.JonesWenzlProjector.mk","kind":"ctor","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTraceOnHecke.lean#L98-L98","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.JonesWenzlProjector","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.JonesWenzlProjector","kind":"class","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTraceOnHecke.lean#L90-L101","doc":"The **Jones-Wenzl projector** `p_n ∈ H_n(q)` is the idempotent\nprojecting onto the (n)-irreducible component.\n\nIdempotence (`p·p = p`) is now **enforced** as a Lean proposition over\nthe `(p : H)` parameter.  The strand-killing relation\n(`p·σ_i = -q⁻¹·p` for `i < n-1`) needs the generators `σ_i` — absent from\nthis class's signature — so it remains documentation for the eventual\ninstance, not an enforced field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovTrace.map_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovTrace.map_smul","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTraceOnHecke.lean#L84-L84","doc":"(M1b) `R`-scalar compatibility — the rest of `R`-linearity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovTrace.map_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovTrace.map_add","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTraceOnHecke.lean#L82-L82","doc":"(M1a) Additivity — part of `R`-linearity of `tr`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovTrace.cyclic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovTrace.cyclic","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTraceOnHecke.lean#L80-L80","doc":"(M2) Conjugation invariance / cyclicity: `tr (x·y) = tr (y·x)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovTrace.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovTrace.mk","kind":"ctor","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTraceOnHecke.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovTrace","kind":"class","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTraceOnHecke.lean#L68-L84","doc":"A **Markov trace** on `H_n(q)` is a linear functional satisfying\nthe Markov reduction property.\n\nTwo of the three Markov laws are now **enforced** as Lean propositions\nover the `(tr : H → R)` parameter (`H` is a `Ring`, `R`-algebra): (M1)\n`R`-linearity of `tr` and (M2) conjugation invariance `tr (x·y) = tr (y·x)`.\nThe third law, (M3) Markov reduction `tr (x·σ_{n-1}) = z·tr (x)`, still\nrequires the generator `σ_{n-1}` — not a parameter of this class — so it\nremains documentation for the eventual instance, not an enforced field. ","signatureChunk":0}]}